        		<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript">
        	function checkChildren(srcObj, vType) {
        		for (var i = 0; i < eval("document.formSMC." + vType + ".length"); i++) {
        			if ((eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].value.substring(0, srcObj.length)") == srcObj) && (eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].disabled") == false)) {
        					(eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].checked")) ? eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = false : eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = true;
        			}
        		}
        		return false;
        	}
        function toggleRepealed(element) {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        		else {
        			row.classList.remove('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        function HideRepealed() {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        </script>
        <div style="padding: 15px;"><form action="/smc/" method="post" name="formSMC">
        <div id="hideRepealed">
        		<p><a href="/smc/?Title=04">Title 04</a> Administrative Agencies and Procedures</p>
        				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.01">Chapter 04.01</a> General Administrative Procedures</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.010">Section 04.01.010</a> Policy on Boards, Commissions and Other Administrative Agencies<br />
        <p>It is the policy of the City to utilize citizen boards, commissions, committees and other groups to aid the process of effective, responsible and efficient government by: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>marshalling and channeling the resources of expertise and insight available in the community to complement the judgment of the council and professional staff;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>providing more available forums for dialog and public hearings;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>providing mechanisms appropriate for the ascertainment of facts and the discernment of views; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>broadening the base of citizen participation in the processes of self-government.</li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.020">Section 04.01.020</a> Purposes<br />
        <p>To the ends declared in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.01.010">SMC 4.01.010</a>, the city council expresses its purpose to: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>people these agencies of government with persons who are qualified by training and experience in the subject matter or fairly representative of the groups interested in the subject matter;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>insist upon willing self-sacrifice and personal integrity such as will sustain these officials above the appearance of impropriety;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>require the necessary effort and attendance at meetings;<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>facilitate the work of such bodies by giving them support and adequate guidance; and<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>protect the members of official agencies from the burdens of liability and other frustrations which might impede conscientious decision making.</li></ol>
        <p>To such extent as is consistent with the statute, ordinance or charter provision creating each board, commission and committee, the City follows the principles set forth in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.01">SMC 4.01.030 through SMC 4.01.090</a>.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.030">Section 04.01.030</a> Appointment<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Appointments to City boards, commissions or agencies made by the City Council are to be made from residents of the City, unless the provision establishing the requirement for the appointment specifically permits or requires the appointment of a nonresident. Any current member of a board, commission or agency who is not a resident of the City shall be permitted to complete his or her term and any subsequent reappointment.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Appointees shall be at least eighteen years of age unless the state law or City ordinance creating the board, commission or agency provides for appointees under the age of eighteen.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Appointees shall have indicated a willingness to serve in such capacity in response to efforts by the mayor to extend the opportunity for service to all concerned citizens and groups so as to achieve the greatest degree of public confidence and&nbsp;expertise.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Unless otherwise specifically prohibited by the document creating the appointment to a City board, commission or agency, the incumbent members appointed by the city council shall continue to serve and remain a voting member beyond the expiration of his or her term until a replacement member has been appointed and assumed the position.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 24, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, May 9, 2014</p><p>ORD C 35084 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.035">Section 04.01.035</a> Removal<br />
        <p>Removal of members of boards, commissions, and committees established by this Title 04 shall be done by Council resolution and according to the standards contained in the code chapter specific to that board, commission or committee.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.040">Section 04.01.040</a> Compatibility of Office<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">No particular kind of private or public employment disqualifies a person from appointment or retention unless the employment can be expected to give rise, in more than an incidental and isolated way, to obligations inconsistent with one&rsquo;s obligations as a member of the agency. However, unless the city council specifically determines in each particular case that special and unusual circumstances exist which justify the appointment to or continuation of an agency, City employees are not to be appointed or reappointed to any agency and any member of an agency who becomes a City employee is not to continue as a member of the agency.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.050">Section 04.01.050</a> Disqualification<br />
        <p>No member of an agency is to participate in the hearing, consideration or decision on a matter under circumstances of actual or apparent bias or partiality arising from close personal, familial or business relationship with interested parties, or a pecuniary interest that could be directly or indirectly affected by the agency’s decision.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.060">Section 04.01.060</a> Attendance<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">Each agency is to specify by rule the procedures whereby the chair determines whether an absence is excused and the attendance of each member at meetings of the agency or committees of the agency is recorded. The chair reports unexcused absences to the mayor. Three consecutive unexcused absences, or absences from twenty-five percent or more of the meetings in a year, is ground for removal of a member.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.070">Section 04.01.070</a> Meetings<br />
        <p>Agencies shall endeavor to hold meetings, particularly where public hearing or citizen input is an important aspect of the action being taken, during weekday evening hours.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.080">Section 04.01.080</a> Rules<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Each board or commission may promulgate rules for the conduct of its business which shall promote the policies and objectives of this chapter; provided, any Public Rule shall be adopted only as set forth in in Chapter 3.14 of the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:5pt; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 24, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Tuesday, January 7, 2025</p><p>ORD C36752 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.01.090">Section 04.01.090</a> Indemnification<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">The City includes the individual members of official City agencies within coverage afforded officers and agents by its insurance program and indemnification policy as set forth in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=03.07">chapter 3.07 SMC</a> to protect and hold them harmless from any action, claim or proceeding against them arising out of the performance or failure of performance of their duties and functions which might result in personal liability, and by such insurance, or through the office of the city attorney, or otherwise, hold them personally harmless from all expenses arising from such claims, in all cases where the members have acted within the scope of their agency in good faith.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.02">Chapter 04.02</a> Special Administrative Procedures – Billing and Collection of Claims</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.160">Section 04.02.160</a> Obligations of Landlords and Sellers<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Property owners derive substantial benefit and value to their property from service from the three municipal utilities being furnished or available to their premises at the lowest cost, even where an owner is not the direct customer. As a condition of continued enjoyment of such benefits, property owners must accept joint and several responsibility for full payment of municipal utility charges to their premises during their time of ownership as well as any additional periods allowed by municipal utility lien rights or as otherwise provided by contract or at law.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A person selling or letting any premises subject to delinquency for municipal utility services shall provide the purchaser or renter, at or before the sale or rental, with a copy of the most recent City utilities bill. A person failing to make such disclosure commits a civil infraction.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Property owners and landlords are required to make provision for the payment of charges regularly listed upon the City utilities bill before transferring ownership or occupancy. Failure to make provisions for payment for utility services at a premises tends to create unhealthful and unsanitary conditions and is a public nuisance. A property owner or landlord failing to make provision for payment of a utility bill prior to transferring ownership or occupancy commits a civil infraction. A thirty-day warning notice, including notice of a right to a hearing on any disputed amounts, shall be given prior to further enforcement action where a prior utility bill has not been regularly furnished to a property owner or landlord.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City utility billings office may seek recovery of all combined utility bill charges in any court of competent jurisdiction against a customer or other responsible party for unpaid charges, including any special charges imposed under&nbsp;</span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.02.120" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 4.02.120</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">, plus any other recoverable costs or fees. As used herein, &ldquo;other responsible person&rdquo; includes the landlord or property owner. Said term additionally may include any tenant or occupant, where such person received the benefit of municipal utility services or otherwise regularly paid or made arrangements to pay municipal utility bills during the period of tenancy or occupancy. (See&nbsp;</span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=13.01.0312" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 13.01.0312</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">)</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director does not terminate water service to a new tenant not otherwise responsible for the bill, so long as the account remains current for payment of services thereafter.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 14, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 24, 2025</p><p>ORD C36702 Section 12</p>						<p>Article I. In General</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.010">Section 04.02.010</a> Policy to Collect Accounts<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">It is the policy of the City to promptly identify and collect all duly payable moneys related to services rendered, damage to City property, or any other source.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">It is the policy of the City to regularly review and, as necessary, adjust schedules for fees, charges, and other assessments to ensure the City recovers at least the actual cost of delivering said services. Accordingly, during the even year of each biennium, all city departments shall review as appropriate their schedules for fees, charges, and other assessments to ensure there is adequate cost recovery for the services rendered and shall then report the status and outcome of such review to the Mayor and City Council.&nbsp; The biennial review and adjustment shall be governed by the following specific criteria:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Except as otherwise provided in this section, fees, charges and assessments shall be adjusted by reference to the&nbsp;Consumer Price Index published by the United States Bureau of Labor Statistics, (All City Average (CPI-U and CPI-W)) or such other applicable index or formula appropriate for the service rendered.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">General facilities charges shall be updated and maintained pursuant to Chapters&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=13.03" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">13.03</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=13.04" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">13.04</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;of the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Transportation impact fees shall be updated and maintained pursuant to Chapter&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=17D.075" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">17D.075</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;of the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This section shall not apply to criminal and civil penalties fees, which shall be adjusted consistent with state law and any penalty schedule established separately under the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In reviewing fees, charges, and other assessments each biennium, each City department shall systematically and resolutely pursue opportunities to maximize operational efficiency, eliminate waste, streamline processes, and minimize administrative costs to ensure the lowest possible financial burden on payers. This includes exploring innovative solutions that enhance effectiveness and reduce expenses. In conjunction with the Information Technology Department, departments shall also evaluate and implement apt software and platforms that automate workflows, improve accuracy, and reduce the costs associated with calculating and billing fees, charges, and other assessments.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Nothing in this section shall be construed to prohibit review and adjustment of fees more frequently than every biennium.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2026</p><p>ORD C36839 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.020">Section 04.02.020</a> Rules and Regulations – General<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City may promulgate rules and regulations for the collection and reporting of all moneys due the City with attendant emphasis on identifying moneys to which the City is entitled, prompt invoicing and reporting among affected departments, and prosecuting delinquencies. The rules and regulations may specify when and how collection is to be affected, negotiation of payments, collection of interest on payments not to exceed the maximum allowed by state law, such other costs as may be incurred by the City due to delinquency, and settlement of claims not to exceed two thousand five hundred dollars in total value before negotiated settlement.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any Public Rule shall be adopted pursuant to Chapter 03.14 of the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 24, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Tuesday, January 7, 2025</p><p>ORD C36752 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.030">Section 04.02.030</a> Filing Claims Against the City<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In specification of chapter 35.31 RCW and <a href="/charter/#Sec115"><span style="color:blue">City Charter Section 115</span></a>, a person seeking to recover monetary damages against the City must file a claim in writing with the city clerk. The claim must state:</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the claimant&rsquo;s name, date of birth and actual residence by street and number;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the claimant&rsquo;s address(es) by street and number for the six months immediately prior to the time the claim accrued;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">a detailed description of the incident giving rise to the claim, including the date, time and place, and how it is believed the City is at fault, including as appropriate:</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">a description of any defect in equipment or premises, and</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">acts or omissions of City agents;</span></span></span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the name, address and telephone number of any third party whose property was damaged in the incident;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the name, address and telephone number of all witnesses and other persons with information about the claim and other persons involved in the incident;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="6">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the dollar amount of the claim and an itemization listing specific losses actually sustained or expected, along with copies of bills, statements, estimates, or other proof of specific losses;</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="7">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">whether the claim may be compromised or settled and, if so, for what amount.</span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The claim must bear an acknowledgement that it has been sworn to or affirmed by the claimant or an authorized representative.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A claim must be filed at least sixty days before the filing of any legal action arising from the incident (or, in the event the statute of limitations would expire within such sixty-day period, at any time prior to filing of the action).</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In the event any provision, sentence, clause or word hereof is held to be invalid or void, it is the intent that the remainder not be affected and remain fully in effect and force as if such invalid or void portion had been eliminated at the time of enactment.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The purposes of this section are to implement the statutory and charter requirements for filing claims and to foster negotiation and settlement of claims, protecting the City&rsquo;s interests without substantially burdening claimants.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.040">Section 04.02.040</a> Industrial Insurance Claims<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Claims for industrial injuries shall be reported and investigated in accordance with administrative rules and regulations promulgated by the mayor. &nbsp;Administrative rules and regulations promulgated pursuant to this section shall not be subject to Chapter 03.14 of the Spokane Municipal Code, unless they apply to persons other than City officers or employees.</span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 24, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Tuesday, January 7, 2025</p><p>ORD C36752 Section 6</p>						<p>Article II. Utilities Billings and Collections</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.050">Section 04.02.050</a> Utilities Billings and Collections – Purpose<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The purpose of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.02"><span style="color:blue">SMC 4.02.060 through SMC 4.02.220</span></a> is to establish procedures regarding utility billing practices of the City, including procedures for termination and resumption of utility services, and to accomplish the prompt and efficient collection of amounts owing on the accounts of public utilities, including water, sewer, solid waste and other matters encompassed by the City&rsquo;s utilities&nbsp;operations.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The provisions of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.02"><span style="color:blue">SMC 4.02.060 through SMC 4.02.220</span></a> are declared to comprise additional terms and conditions of service and a basis of the contract under which municipal utilities extend service to customers and for the benefit of property owners of premises receiving such service under <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Title=13"><span style="color:blue">Title 13 SMC</span></a>.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.060">Section 04.02.060</a> Definitions<br />
        <p>For the purposes of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.02">SMC 4.02.060 through SMC 4.02.220</a>, the following words are defined as follows: </p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>“Customer” means the municipal utility rate-payer, as identified by the utility account billing address shown in the files of the City utilities billing office.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>“Director” means the director of public works and utilities.</li></ol>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.070">Section 04.02.070</a> Rules and Regulations<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The City has authority to promulgate rules and regulations, develop administrative procedures and do all things necessary to effectuate the purposes of <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.02.060">SMC 4.02.060</a> through <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.02.220">SMC 4.02.220</a>. Any Public Rule shall be adopted pursuant to Chapter 03.14 of the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 24, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Tuesday, January 7, 2025</p><p>ORD C36752 Section 7</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.080">Section 04.02.080</a> Billing Cycle<br />
        <p>Unless otherwise directed for administrative convenience and efficiency by the director, billings are issued on a monthly cycle, water consumption being billed bimonthly. Current charges are itemized for water, sewer and refuse services and other items as the director may prescribe. Past due charges may be shown as a single delinquent balance.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.090">Section 04.02.090</a> Allocation of Payments<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>The city council finds that City utility customers and property owners receive substantial benefit and convenience of a combined utilities billing system. This policy results in lower utility rates and reduced losses from nonpayment, so that the payment allocation policy specified herein should be adopted and enforced as a condition of access to municipal utility services.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>Utility bill payments received are allocated to charges in this order of priority: labor and materials, additional refuse, refuse, additional sewer, sewer, and water. In case of a dispute on one part of a bill, the undisputed portion must be paid. A customer may allocate a partial payment in order to avoid termination of a specific utility service.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.100">Section 04.02.100</a> Estimates<br />
        <p>Billings for utilities may be based upon reasonable estimations from prior consumption, comparable usages, estimated costs of other services, or other bases.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.110">Section 04.02.110</a> Readings by Customer<br />
        <p>The director may provide, in lieu of reading by City meter readers, for the distribution of mail-in cards and procedures for customers to telephone meter readings.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.120">Section 04.02.120</a> Special Charges<br />
        <p>The director may establish charges for handling dishonored checks, drafts, money orders or other instruments; fees for turning water on or off; and charges for delinquent accounts.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.130">Section 04.02.130</a> Advance Payment and Security<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">The director may require new or existing customers to make advance payment or noninterest-bearing security deposit to insure payment for utility services, labor, materials or other items when warranted by such circumstances as the nature of the charge, the amount of the charge, past delinquency or other evidence of the customer&rsquo;s inability or unwillingness to pay promptly utility charges owing or to become owing.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.140">Section 04.02.140</a> Time for Payment<br />
        <p><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director establishes the period for payment of utility bills, which is at least twenty days after date of issuance of the bill.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 4, 2019</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, March 15, 2019</p><p>ORD C35737 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.150">Section 04.02.150</a> Deferred Payment of Delinquent Accounts<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director, by regulation, establishes a procedure whereby termination of service is delayed upon condition that the customer enter into a deferred payment agreement. The director takes into account in establishing the terms of the agreement whether the account is residential or commercial, the size of the delinquency, the customer&rsquo;s ability to pay and payment history, the length of time the account has been delinquent, the reasons for the delinquency and any other relevant&nbsp;circumstances.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director may refuse to enter into a deferred payment agreement with a customer who has defaulted on a previous agreement.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.170">Section 04.02.170</a> Billings Examiner<br />
        <p>The director provides procedures, facilities and direction for the water billings examiner(s) who receives inquiries, conducts informal hearings and resolves disputes of customers about billings when the City asserts a right to terminate service for nonpayment of charges. The examiner does not participate in delinquent payment negotiations.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.180">Section 04.02.180</a> Notice of Termination<br />
        <p>Prior to termination of water service because of nonpayment the director causes notice to be given as prescribed in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.02.190">SMC 4.02.190</a>. Notice is not required of service termination at the request or with the consent of the customer, necessary for repair, in an emergency or for any other reason.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.190">Section 04.02.190</a> Notice of Termination – Form and Service<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>An initial delinquency notice is given which includes substantially the following information:
        <p align="center"><b>DELINQUENT NOTICE </b></p>
        <p>YOUR CITY WATER SERVICE WILL BE TERMINATED unless all amounts not disputed are paid. You may make arrangements to pay the delinquent amount by phoning or writing: </p>
        <p>CITY UTILITIES BILLING CREDIT OFFICE<br />Phone (509) 625-6006<br />City Hall<br />808 West Spokane Falls Boulevard<br />Spokane, WA 99201 </p>
        <p>This office is open every business day from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. If you dispute any amounts due, you may request an informal dispute hearing by visiting, phoning or writing: </p>
        <p>City Water Billings Examiner<br />Phone (509) 625-6000<br />City Hall<br />808 West Spokane Falls Boulevard<br />Spokane, WA 99201 </p>
        <p>This office is open every City business day from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Your request for a hearing must be received by the City Water Billings Examiner within five business days. </p>
        <p>Note: IF SERVICE IS TERMINATED, A RECONNECTION FEE WILL BE CHARGED. A COLLECTION FEE WILL BE CHARGED FOR DELINQUENT ACCOUNT COLLECTION EFFORTS AT THE PROPERTY. PROMPT PAYMENT OF YOUR UTILITIES BILL AT THE UTILITIES BILLING OFFICE WILL SAVE YOU AND THE UTILITIES BILLING DIVISION EXPENSE AND ANNOYANCE.<br />&nbsp;</p></li>
        <li>The information may be disclosed with the bill, delivered personally, given orally or left or posted at the billing address as shown in the City’s utility billings files.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>In the event an account remains unpaid, a second or final notice is given to the service address. The notice may be given orally to an occupant or left or posted at the service address as shown in the City’s utility billings files. The notice includes the following information:
        <p>SERVICES ARE SUBJECT TO TERMINATION AFTER FIVE BUSINESS DAYS FROM DATE OF THIS NOTICE. SERVICE WILL NOT BE RESTORED WITHOUT FULL PAYMENT PLUS TURN-ON FEE. A COLLECTION CHARGE WILL BE INCURRED IF A COLLECTOR IS REQUIRED TO COME TO THE PROPERTY. </p>
        <p>If you dispute any amounts due, you may request an informal dispute hearing by visiting, phoning or writing: </p>
        <p>City Water Billings Examiner<br />Phone (509) 625-6000<br />City Hall<br />808 West Spokane Falls Boulevard<br />Spokane, WA 99201 </p>
        <p>This office is open every City business day from 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Your request for a hearing must be received by the City water billings examiner within five business days. </p>
        <p>FOR ARRANGEMENTS, PHONE OR COME TO UTILITIES BILLING DIVISION – CREDIT OFFICE<br />(509) 625-6006<br />TDD (For Hearing Impaired) (509) 625-6683 </p>
        <p>IF PAYMENT OR ARRANGEMENTS HAVE BEEN MADE, YOU MAY DISREGARD THIS NOTICE. Arrangements must be kept to avoid termination of service.</p></li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.200">Section 04.02.200</a> Utility Lien – Additional<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">The City has a lien against premises receiving water utility services, for up to four months&rsquo; water utility charges, enforceable by termination of service, all as provided in RCW 35.21.290 and RCW 35.21.300. This is not by way of limitation of the right to terminate service for nonpayment, but service will not be denied to new tenants accepting responsibility for their utility service or new property owners beyond accrued rights under contract or statute.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.210">Section 04.02.210</a> Delegation by Director<br />
        <p>The director may delegate such authority as is deemed necessary.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.02.220">Section 04.02.220</a> Provisions Cumulative<br />
        <p>The provisions of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=04.02">SMC 4.02.050 through SMC 4.02.210</a> do not limit but are in addition to all other powers, rights and remedies the City may have.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.05">Chapter 04.05</a> Arts Commission</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.010">Section 04.05.010</a> Purpose<br />
        <p>In recognition of the facts that artists and artistic institutions of Spokane contribute to and provide cultural, educational, entertainment and recreational benefits available to and used by the citizens of Spokane and enhance the public environment and welfare, the Spokane arts commission is established to promote and encourage public programs to further the development of public awareness of and interest in the fine and performing arts and preservation of the cultural heritage of the City in connection with the artistic and cultural development of the City.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.020">Section 04.05.020</a> Appointment<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The Arts Commission consists of sixteen (16) members nominated by the Mayor and appointed by the City Council to staggered three-year terms. The membership shall be composed of two<strong>&nbsp;</strong>members residing in each of the council districts. The remaining ten positions shall be designated as at-large positions and shall be filled by qualified city residents regardless of the council district in which they reside.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Vacancies are filled by appointments to unexpired terms in the same manner.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The City Council may appoint a city council member to serve as a liaison to the Arts Commission.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 30, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 13, 2026</p><p>ORD C36849 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.025">Section 04.05.025</a> Removal<br />
        <p>Commission members shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of their terms except for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No commission member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.030">Section 04.05.030</a> Officers<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The Arts Commission by rule determines its officers and the manner of their selection.</span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 30, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 13, 2026</p><p>ORD C36849 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.040">Section 04.05.040</a> Duties and Functions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The Arts Commission has the power and duty to:</span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">adopt rules;</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">hold regular public meetings and keep a written record of its proceedings which is a public record;</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">initiate, sponsor or conduct, alone or in cooperation with other public or private agencies, public programs to further the development and public awareness of, and interest in, the fine and performing arts, and preservation of the cultural heritage of the City;</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">encourage donations and grants to the City for civic arts purposes, to advise the City regarding the receipt of such donations and grants and transmit any funds so received to the City;</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">advise the City concerning the receipt of or purchase of works of art to be placed on municipal property;</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">advise and assist the City in connection with such other artistic and heritage activities as may be referred to it by the City.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">establish an annual work plan in consultation with the appropriate City staff designated by the Mayor, which shall be adopted by the City Council</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 30, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, May 13, 2026</p><p>ORD C36849 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.050">Section 04.05.050</a> REPEALED (Municipal Arts Plan)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Wednesday, July 22, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 23, 2026</p><p>ORD C36892 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.060">Section 04.05.060</a> Commission Review of Proposals<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The commission reviews and makes recommendations to the council regarding:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the implementation of municipal art projects, as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=07.06.400"><span style="color:blue">SMC 7.06.400</span></a>;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">every proposal to procure or place tangible art work on City property;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the interior and exterior of City structures;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the removal, relocation, or alteration of existing municipal art work.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The commission may upon request provide comment upon the arts activities of the park board and the library board.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.05.070">Section 04.05.070</a> “Art” Defined<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>For the purposes of <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.05.040">SMC 4.05.040(E)</a>, <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.05.050">SMC 4.05.050</a> and <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=07.06.400">SMC 7.06.400</a>, “art” means visual art, including sculpture, painting, weaving, photography, print-making, drawing, calligraphy and the fine crafts.<br />&nbsp; 
        <li>For the general purposes of the commission, such as provided in <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.05.040">SMC 4.05.040(C), (D) and (F)</a>, “art” includes not only visual art but also literary and performing arts, such as dramatic, comedic and musical theater, dance, music, poetry and other creative writing.</li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.06">Chapter 04.06</a> REPEALED (Building and Construction Boards and Hearings)</p>
        						<p>Article I. Construction Review Board</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.010">Section 04.06.010</a> REPEALED (Purpose)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.020">Section 04.06.020</a> REPEALED (Members)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.030">Section 04.06.030</a> REPEALED (Appointment)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.035">Section 04.06.035</a> REPEALED (Initial Appointments)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.036">Section 04.06.036</a> REPEALED (Removal)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.040">Section 04.06.040</a> REPEALED (Meetings)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.050">Section 04.06.050</a> REPEALED (Decisions Final)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.060">Section 04.06.060</a> REPEALED (Rules and Regulations)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>						<p>Article II. Board of Boiler Examiners</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.110">Section 04.06.110</a> REPEALED (Created)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.120">Section 04.06.120</a> REPEALED (Members)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.125">Section 04.06.125</a> REPEALED (Removal)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.130">Section 04.06.130</a> REPEALED (Meetings)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.140">Section 04.06.140</a> REPEALED (Decisions Final)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>						<p>Article III. Board of Heating Mechanical Examiners</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.150">Section 04.06.150</a> REPEALED (Created)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.160">Section 04.06.160</a> REPEALED (Members)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.170">Section 04.06.170</a> REPEALED (Meetings)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.06.180">Section 04.06.180</a> REPEALED (Decisions Final)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 20, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, June 27, 2024</p><p>ORD C36519 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.07">Chapter 04.07</a> Civil Service Commission</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.07.010">Section 04.07.010</a> Compensation<br />
        <p>As authorized by <a href="/charter/#Sec52">Charter Section 52(a)</a> civil service commissioners receive compensation of thirty-five dollars per month.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.07.020">Section 04.07.020</a> Removal<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">The commission member appointed by the City Council pursuant to section 52 of the City Charter shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of his or her term except for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No commission member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 5</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.10">Chapter 04.10</a> Human Rights Commission</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.10.010">Section 04.10.010</a> Purpose<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The human rights commission advises and makes recommendations to the city council regarding issues related to human rights and unjust discrimination and the implementation of programs consistent with the needs of all residents of the City of&nbsp;Spokane. The commission shall review all proposed ordinances modifying or expanding the provisions of Title 18 of the Spokane Municipal Code, as well as other provisions of the Spokane Municipal Code that regulate discriminatory practices and claims.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, September 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36716 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.10.020">Section 04.10.020</a> Appointment<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The commission consists of twelve voting members nominated by the mayor and appointed by the city council to staggered three-year terms commencing on the date of appointment.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Membership shall be composed of one<strong> </strong>member residing in each of the council districts. The remaining six positions shall be designated as at-large positions and shall be filled by qualified City residents regardless of the council district in which they reside. </span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In addition to the nine positions set forth in Subsection (B), three additional positions may be filled with youth representatives, with no more than one youth representative residing in each of the council districts. The youth representative positions shall be open to any person under the age of eighteen for a term of one year commencing on the date of appointment, with the option of reappointment to additional one-year terms if the person has not reached the age of eighteen or is enrolled in high school at the time the previous term expires.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Vacancies for all positions are filled by appointment to unexpired terms, after which the member may be reappointed to a subsequent term in the same manner.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 30, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, November 7, 2024</p><p>ORD C36578 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.10.025">Section 04.10.025</a> Removal<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">Board members shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of their terms except for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No board member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.10.030">Section 04.10.030</a> Offices<br />
        <p>The commission by rule determines its officers and the manner of their selection except that the mayor nominates and the city council appoints the chair of the commission, who is recommended by the members of the commission, for a term of one year.</p>
        <p>Applications for the Human Rights Commission shall be forwarded to the members of the commission upon receipt of them from the Mayor’s office.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 29, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, November 15, 2014</p><p>ORD C35154 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.10.040">Section 04.10.040</a> Duties and Functions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The commission has the power and duty to:</span></span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">adopt rules;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">hold regular public meetings and keep a written record of its proceedings which is a public record;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">serve as a complaint channel to which human rights grievances of all types can be reported;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">maintain statistical data on incidents of human rights violations and make appropriate recommendations for correction;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">conduct public hearings to receive citizen concerns about issues relating to human rights;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">conduct and arrange for surveys, studies, and polls to factually determine problem areas and perceptions;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">provide conflict management and dispute resolution services such as conciliation and mediation;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">provide and arrange for victim assistance and support groups;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-roman">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">convene and develop work groups such as sub-committees, ad hoc committees, task forces, and coalitions consisting of concerned organizations, agencies, and individuals to achieve coordinated focus on priority problem areas;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="10" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">provide and develop community education projects such as conferences, forums, and workshops in collaboration and co-sponsorship with organizations and other agencies;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="11" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">conduct diversity training programs for public and private employers, citizen groups and agencies;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="12" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">create a speaker&rsquo;s bureau to address cultural diversity issues;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="13" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">publish a periodic newsletter on current events and special reports on studies and related findings and recommendations;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="14" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">develop a mass media program consisting of the appropriate use of press releases, press conferences, public service announcements, and production;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="15" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">make recommendations for public policy relating to human rights;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="16" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">issue quarterly reports to the City Council concerning the number of complaints received by the City, the number and type of complaints referred to other entities by the name of the entity, the number of complaints dismissed by the City without either investigation or referral, the number of complaints referred by the City to mediation and the number and type of results of those mediations, the number of complaints referred to the City Prosecutor and the resulting outcomes, and any other actions which the City Council determines to be helpful, provided that in no event will such reports contain personally-identifying information; and</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="17" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">issue an annual report to the mayor and city council on the health of human rights along with achievements for the past year and goals for the coming year; and</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="18" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">provide guidance for the city&rsquo;s anti-discrimination efforts without limitation, including&nbsp;federal Title VI compliance efforts; and</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="19" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">review and comment on proposed ordinances amending Title 18 of the Spokane Municipal Code as well as other provisions of the Spokane Municipal Code that regulate discriminatory practices and claims. The Commission shall be provided a draft copy of each ordinance prior to appearing on a Council committee agenda. The Commission may submit its written comments to the Council at any time before final action by the Council on such applicable ordinance. The Council may bypass this requirement pursuant to <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=01.01.080">Section 01.01.080</a> of the Spokane Municipal Code.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0.5in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, September 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36716 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.10.050">Section 04.10.050</a> Complaint evaluation process<br />
        <p>
        	Complaints of alleged human rights violations received by the commission shall be evaluated according to the process set forth in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=18.01.050" target="_blank">SMC 18.01.050</a>.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 27, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 13, 2017</p><p>ORD C35485 Section 5</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.11">Chapter 04.11</a> Park Board</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.11.010">Section 04.11.010</a> Authority<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">The park board has authority, consistent with the charter and ordinances of Spokane, to adopt, promulgate and enforce rules and regulations respecting the management, control and use of all public squares and parks, park drives, parkways, boulevards, play and recreation grounds and facilities, including the fixing and collecting of fees, rents and charges.<br />
        	&nbsp;</li>
        	<li style="text-align: justify;">While the city treasurer is the custodian of the park fund, the director of parks and recreation and the park board, respectively, have the authority over the park fund that the mayor and city council have over all other funds and may expend the park fund in accordance with its appropriations. The monthly and annual reports called for by <a href="/charter/#Sec45">Charter Section 45</a> will continue to be made to the city council.</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.11.015">Section 04.11.015</a> Park Board – Term of Office<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Notwithstanding any other provision of law, a park board member whose term has expired may not continue to serve after expiration of the member&rsquo;s term.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 13, 2022</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, July 17, 2022</p><p>ORD C36218 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.11.020">Section 04.11.020</a> Removal<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">Pursuant to section 41 of the City Charter, board members shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of their terms except for a disqualifying change of residence, for excessive absences as described in section 43 of the City Charter, or for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No board member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 8</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.12">Chapter 04.12</a> Plan Commission</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.010">Section 04.12.010</a> Purpose<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Pursuant to <a href="/charter/"><span style="color:blue">Charter sections 126 through 128</span></a>, there shall be a City plan commission (referred to in this chapter as the &quot;commission&quot;). In addition to exercising those powers granted to the commission in section 128 of the City&rsquo;s Charter, the commission shall provide advice and make recommendation on broad planning goals and policies and on whichever plans for the physical development of the City that the city council may request the commission&#39;s advice by ordinance or resolution.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The functions of the commission shall be advisory only.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The commission shall provide opportunities for public participation in City planning by:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">providing through its own broadly based membership an informed opinion to complement the work of the City&#39;s elected officials and administrative departments;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">soliciting public comment, when pertinent, on planning issues of City-wide importance or of a substantial community concern, and evaluating comments received; and</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">securing the assistance of experts and others with knowledge or ideas to contribute to City planning.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Without limiting the generality of subsections (A) and (C ) of this section, the commission shall hold public hearings and make recommendations to the city council regarding the following matters:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Amendments to the City&rsquo;s comprehensive plan and the development regulations implementing the comprehensive plan.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Changes in the corporate limits of the City, including the land use designations and zoning to become effective upon the annexation of any area proposed for annexation or which might reasonably be expected to be annexed by the City at any future time.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Meetings of the commission, the minutes of its proceedings, and its findings and recommendations shall be open to the public.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2009</p><p>ORD C34403 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.020">Section 04.12.020</a> Membership<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">The commission shall consist of ten members, who shall serve without compensation. The membership as a whole shall reflect a broad range of opinion, experience, and expertise with the objective of providing sound advice representative of the citizenry. To achieve that purpose, it shall include residents from diverse neighborhoods and council districts within the City with diverse professional backgrounds and citizens active in neighborhood or community affairs.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2009</p><p>ORD C34403 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.030">Section 04.12.030</a> Appointment and Term<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Appointment.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Members are nominated by the mayor and appointed by a majority of the city council.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All commission members shall be qualified electors of the City.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Term.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The term of office shall be four years. The terms of two of the members shall expire every odd-numbered year. The terms of three of the members shall expire every even-numbered year. The mayor may nominate and a majority of the city council may appoint existing and newly appointed members to such shorter and/or longer terms as are necessary to achieve this term cycle.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A commission member whose term has expired shall continue to hold office until a successor has qualified, but no more than ninety days.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No member shall serve more than two consecutive terms.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Vacancy.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any vacancy shall be filled for an unexpired term in the same manner as for an original appointment under this section as amended.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Appointment to fill the balance of an unexpired term where more than half of the unexpired term remains shall be considered a full term.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The director of planning and economic development services shall provide written notice at least sixty days but not more than one hundred twenty days prior to the expiration of every commission member term. The notice shall be provided to the commission president, the commission member whose term is expiring, and the mayor.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 9, 2012</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, February 16, 2012</p><p>ORD C34824 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.035">Section 04.12.035</a> Removal<br />
        <p>Commission members shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of their terms except for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No commission member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 9</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.040">Section 04.12.040</a> Liaison Members<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The City Council shall appoint one City Council member to serve as a liaison to the Plan Commission and shall also appoint an alternate City Council member to serve in the absence of the liaison.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The Community Assembly shall nominate a qualified neighborhood council member to serve as a liaison to the Plan Commission, subject to confirmation by the Mayor and appointment by the City Council. Additionally, the Community Assembly may nominate an additional qualified neighborhood council member to serve as a liaison to the Plan Commission&rsquo;s Design Review Subcommittee, subject to confirmation by the Mayor and appointment by the City Council.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The liaison members shall be non-voting participants in commission business.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.050">Section 04.12.050</a> Ancillary Powers<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The plan commission shall have the power to:</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">select one member as the president of the commission for a term of two years. No person shall serve as president for more than two consecutive terms;</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">organize itself, establish committees or subcommittees, establish annual work programs in consultation with the director of planning and economic development services, and delegate duties for the performance of its work;</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">adopt rules of procedure to accomplish its functions and to provide in such rules for the time and place for holding regular Commission meetings;</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">use administrative support and staff provided by the planning and economic development services department as well as technical support from other appropriate City departments and offices as necessary to assist the commission in the performance of its functions, maintenance of its records, and preparation of official correspondence.</span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2009</p><p>ORD C34403 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.060">Section 04.12.060</a> Temporary Participants<br />
        <p>
        <ol type="A">
        <li>The mayor, city council, or commission may assign one or more persons to sit with and participate in the proceedings of any committee of the commission while considering a specific matter as deemed appropriate to provide expertise or a viewpoint. No such person shall be considered to be a member of the commission or have any authority to vote, and the person's participation shall cease upon completion of the assignment.<br />&nbsp;</li>
        <li>A temporary participant shall not engage in conduct prohibited by the City's code of ethics. </li></ol>
        <p></p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2009</p><p>ORD C34403 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.070">Section 04.12.070</a> Focus of Activities<br />
        <p>It is the intention of the City's legislative authority that the commission direct its activities toward providing recommendations on those broad planning goals and policies and plans for the physical development of the City as identified by the city council as matters for its attention, by ordinance or resolution.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2009</p><p>ORD C34403 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.080">Section 04.12.080</a> Duties<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">Work Plan.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The City Council will, by resolution, adopt a Work Plan which assigns certain policy and planning issues for consideration of the Plan Commission.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The Work Plan may be amended by resolution periodically for the removal of completed tasks and the addition of new ones.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">Emergency or Interim Council Action.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The City Council may, by ordinance, amend the Unified Development Code without review by the Plan Commission and without following other procedures in&nbsp;<a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.025.010" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 17G.025.010</a>. Such action shall be limited to emergency actions necessary to preserve the immediate health and safety of residents, or to interim zoning controls or moratoria for which a work plan is established pursuant to RCW 36.70A.390. All such action shall provide public notice and solicit public comment as appropriate and required by City and state law.</span></p>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Design Review</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:40px; margin-right:0in"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The Plan Commission shall conduct the Standard Design Review process as described in SMC Chapter 17G.041.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.085">Section 04.12.085</a> Design Review<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The Plan Commission shall review projects required to follow the Standard Design Review process provided in the Unified Development Code. Such a review shall be permitted to occur through a Design Review Subcommittee established by the Plan Commission.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The Plan Commission may convene a subcommittee on an ad hoc basis to conduct the Standard Design Review process. The Plan Commission may appoint Plan Commission members to the Design Review Subcommittee on a standing or ad hoc basis. The Design Review Subcommittee shall include the Plan Commission&rsquo;s Community Assembly liaison or an additional qualified neighborhood council member to serve as a liaison to the Plan Commission&rsquo;s Design Review Subcommittee.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">The Plan Commission may appoint design professionals to the Design Review Subcommittee, including but not limited to architects, landscape architects, urban designers, civil/structural engineers, real estate developers, and members of the building trades, to assist in the review of the project subject to Standard Design Review.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#030303">Any meeting of the Plan Commission&rsquo;s Design Review Subcommittee shall be subject to the Open Public Meetings Act under RCW 42.30.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.12.090">Section 04.12.090</a> Unexcused Absences<br />
        <p>A commission member may be removed from office for cause if absent from three consecutive commission meetings or six regularly scheduled meetings in any twelve-month period.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 2, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, April 8, 2009</p><p>ORD C34403 Section 9</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.13">Chapter 04.13</a> Design Review Board (REPEALED)</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.010">Section 04.13.010</a> REPEALED (General)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 14, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, January 16, 2010</p><p>Ordinance C34527 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.015">Section 04.13.015</a> REPEALED (Design Review Board)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.020">Section 04.13.020</a> REPEALED (Authority)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, December 14, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, January 16, 2010</p><p>Ordinance C34527 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.025">Section 04.13.025</a> REPEALED (Composition and Qualification)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.030">Section 04.13.030</a> REPEALED (Appointment and Removal)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.040">Section 04.13.040</a> REPEALED (Terms of Office)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.13.050">Section 04.13.050</a> REPEALED (Design Review Board Administration and Procedures)<br />
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, February 9, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, March 19, 2026</p><p>ORD C36830 Section 4</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.14">Chapter 04.14</a> Retirement and Pension Boards</p>
        						<p>Article I. Fire and Police Pension Boards</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.010">Section 04.14.010</a> Fire Pension Board<br />
        <p>There is established a municipal firemen’s pension board, consisting of the mayor or a council member designated by the mayor, the city clerk or comptroller, the city treasurer, and two regularly employed firefighters, as provided in the Firemen’s Relief and Pension Act of 1947 (RCW 41.16.020), as amended.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.020">Section 04.14.020</a> Police Pension Board<br />
        <p>There is established a board of trustees of the relief and pension fund of the police department, consisting of the mayor or a council member designated by the mayor, the city clerk, the city treasurer, the mayor pro tem and three members of the police department, as provided in RCW 41.20.010.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>						<p>Article II. Spokane Employees' Retirement System Board</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.030">Section 04.14.030</a> Board of Administration<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">There is created a board of administration to administer the retirement system and the retirement fund for superannuated or disabled employees and elected officials of the City, except police and fire department employees entitled to benefits under state&nbsp;law.</span></span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 31, 2014</p><p>ORD C35129 Section 2</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.040">Section 04.14.040</a> Membership – Selection<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The board consists of nine (9) members.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Three (3) board members are appointed by the city council. One of the board member appointments is a council member.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">four (4) board members are elected from employees eligible for the retirement system by such eligible employees; </span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">One (1) board member, the Mayor or the Mayor&rsquo;s designee.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">One (1) board member, who may not be an elected official or employee of the City, is appointed by the other eight (8) board members.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Terms</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The board members appointed by the city council serve at the pleasure of the city council.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The elected employee board members serve staggered four-year terms commencing on the first Monday in July.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The Mayor or designee serves at the discretion of the Mayor during the Mayor&rsquo;s term of office.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The ninth board member serves a four-year term. </span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="5">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">A vacancy is filled and a replacement is made in the same manner as original selections, except that a vacancy in one of the elected employee positions is filled by appointment by the other three (or a minimum of two) elected employee board members, which appointment is until the next annual election.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, August 19, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, September 25, 2024</p><p>ORD C36559 Section 1</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.045">Section 04.14.045</a> Removal<br />
        <p style="text-align:justify">Board members appointed by the City Council pursuant to SMC 04.14.040(A)(1) shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of their terms except for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No board member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 11</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.050">Section 04.14.050</a> Election<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The city clerk conducts an election each year to elect one employee to the board and to elect an employee to an unexpired term, if any.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Candidates for the board are determined by nomination in the form of a notice of nomination signed by at least twenty (20) employees of the City who are members of the retirement system.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An employee may sign more than one nomination.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The city clerk gives notice of the dates for filing notices of nomination and of the election by posting in a prominent place in the city clerk&rsquo;s office. Notices are posted at least thirty (30) days prior to the date nominations are to be received and at least thirty (30) days prior to the date of the election.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Nominations must be received by the second Tuesday in April and the election shall be held on the second Tuesday in May.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The city clerk causes absentee ballots to be printed and available the last week in April. Absentee ballots are accepted up to the date of election and are counted with the ballots regularly cast on election day.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The city clerk causes written ballots containing the names of all persons regularly nominated to be furnished and provides ballot boxes. The city clerk may appoint any City employees as deputies to conduct the election.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The election is held in the city clerk&rsquo;s office and in such other places as the city clerk may designate. The city clerk appoints two employees of the City as officials of said election, who shall be allowed their regular wages for said day, but shall receive no additional compensation therefor.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Employees may vote between the hours of seven-thirty a.m. and five-thirty p.m. on the day fixed by the city clerk for the election. Each employee of the City who is a member of the retirement system is entitled to vote at said election for one person for each board position. The person receiving the highest number of votes is elected to the board.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 31, 2014</p><p>ORD C35129 Section 4</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.060">Section 04.14.060</a> Officers<br />
        <p>The board elects its chairman and secretary.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 31, 2014</p><p>ORD C35129 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.070">Section 04.14.070</a> Powers and Duties<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The board administers the retirement system and the retirement fund under the provisions of ordinance and the direction of the city council.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The board keeps such data in such form as necessary for actuarial valuation of the fund. At least every five (5) years the board causes to be made an actuarial investigation into the mortality and service and compensation experience of retirement system members and beneficiaries, and an actuarial valuation of the assets and liabilities of the fund.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The board transmits to the city council a report of the actuarial investigation and valuation and an annual report on the financial condition of the fund.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">With the approval of the city council, the board may:</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">change the rate of interest on contributions made to the retirement fund;</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">adopt mortality, service and other tables used by the retirement system for the purposes of retirement benefit calculations; and</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">change the rates of contribution to the retirement fund by retirement system members based on such tables.</span></span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Subject to state law, the board provides for the proper investment of the moneys in the retirement fund.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The board adopts rules and regulations as necessary for the administration of the retirement system and retirement fund.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The board may authorize the retirement system director to execute contracts approved by the board. The board does not require city council action to let contracts within the scope of its substantive powers, where such contracts do not impact municipal general fund monies.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 31, 2014</p><p>ORD C35129 Section 6</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=04.14.080">Section 04.14.080</a> Interest of Members<br />
        <p>No board member may have any interest in the making of investments from the retirement fund or in the gains or profits therefrom. No board member may become an endorser, surety or otherwise an obligor for moneys invested in the retirement fund by the board, or borrow any of the retirement system&rsquo;s funds or deposits, or use any of the retirement system&rsquo;s moneys except as directed by the board.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, July 28, 2014</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, August 31, 2014</p><p>ORD C35129 Section 7</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.15">Chapter 04.15</a> REPEALED (Sports, Entertainment, Arts and Convention Advisory Board (SEACAB))</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.15.010">Section 04.15.010</a> REPEALED (Purpose)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C33644.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.15.020">Section 04.15.020</a> REPEALED (Members – Appointment)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C33644.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.15.030">Section 04.15.030</a> REPEALED (Officers)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C33644.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.15.040">Section 04.15.040</a> REPEALED (Meetings)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C33644.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.16">Chapter 04.16</a> Bicycle Advisory Board</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.010">Section 04.16.010</a> Findings<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The City of Spokane finds that:</span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">it is an indisputable fact of urban life that the bicycle is a popular and viable means of personal transportation;</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">the role of the bicycle as a mode of personal transportation in Spokane will continue to increase in importance in coming years;</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">many Spokane residents use their bicycles to commute to work and school, on recreational trips<u>,</u> and for other essential transportation purposes;</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">the City has adopted a Bicycle Master Plan and Bicycle Priority Network to serve as a guide in all matters relating to bicycling;</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">traffic congestion, increasing costs of car ownership, and concern for personal health and air quality have combined to make the bicycle an increasingly attractive transportation option;</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">the active involvement of community members in advising municipal authorities is vital to ensure proper development of the bicycling environment; and</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">promoting the safety and well-being of those who use bicycles for all transportation purposes is a public purpose of the City;</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.020">Section 04.16.020</a> General Purpose<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The Bicycle Advisory Board is established to provide recommendations to the Transportation Commission to advise the Mayor, the City Council, and departments and offices of the City on matters relating to bicycling and to raise public awareness of bicycling issues.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.030">Section 04.16.030</a> Specific Functions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">Without limiting&nbsp;the&nbsp;scope of&nbsp;<a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.16.020" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 4.16.020</a><u>,</u>&nbsp;the Bicycle Advisory Board is given the following functions and responsibilities:</span></span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">To initiate and/or assist in revisions to the City&rsquo;s Bicycle Master Plan.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">To review proposals and plans for spot improvements, street vacations, and bikeways<u>,</u> and provide timely comments to the Transportation Commission and affected agencies.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">To review, evaluate<u>,</u> and comment on the annual six-year bikeways program.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">To promote bicycling as a viable form of urban transportation.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">To promote improved safety to reduce accidents and thefts of bicycles by evaluating and recommending changes in design standards for on-street and off-street bikeways, trails and paths accessible to bicyclists, and for secured bicycle parking.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:10.0pt">To develop possible demonstration projects to encourage commuting through provision of safe, accessible routes, secure bike parking facilities and facilities for commuter clean-up and changing from riding to work clothes.</span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:142.45pt; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.040">Section 04.16.040</a> Membership<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The Bicycle Advisory Board has ten (10) members appointed by the City Council according to the procedures of&nbsp;<a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.01.030" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 4.01.030</a>. An eleventh member between the ages of sixteen and twenty-two may be appointed to the board.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:142.45pt; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.045">Section 04.16.045</a> Removal<br />
        <p>Board members appointed by the City Council pursuant to <a target="_blank" href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=04.16.040">SMC 04.16.040 </a>shall not be removed from office by the City Council before the expiration of their terms except for cause based upon a determination of incapacity, incompetence, the presence of irreconcilable conflicts of interest, neglect of duty, or malfeasance, and upon the affirmative vote of five (5) Council members. No board member shall be removed without written notice of the intent to remove and an opportunity to provide a written response to the notice.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, May 14, 2018</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, June 30, 2018</p><p>ORD C35620 Section 12</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.050">Section 04.16.050</a> Terms<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">Members of the board are appointed to two-year terms.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">No member may serve more than four consecutive full, two-year terms or eight total years.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The eleventh voting member shall serve for a one-year term and may serve two consecutive terms.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.060">Section 04.16.060</a> Compensation<br />
        <p>Members serve without compensation.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 26, 2007</p><p>Effective Date: Sunday, May 6, 2007</p><p>Recodification ORD C33995 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.070">Section 04.16.070</a> Officers<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The board on an annual basis, elects a chair and a vice chair from its membership to preside over meetings and perform such other functions as may be prescribed by rule. </span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.080">Section 04.16.080</a> Staff Support<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The Mayor or Mayor&rsquo;s designee assigns a City employee to provide technical and administrative assistance to the board.</span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:142.45pt; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 7</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=04.16.090">Section 04.16.090</a> Meetings<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">The board meets at least once a month at a prescribed day and time as noticed on the Board agenda. </span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">A quorum is a simple majority of the current board membership.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">All meetings are held in accordance with the Open Public Meetings Act, chapter 42.30 RCW. Minutes of all meetings are kept as public records.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:142.45pt; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 26, 2026</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, March 4, 2026</p><p>ORD C36822 Section 8</p>				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=04.20">Chapter 04.20</a> REPEALED (Emergency Medical Services Advisory Board)</p>
